    "answer": {
      "short": "The events are independent because $P(\\bar T\\mid M)=P(\\bar T)=0.4$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(\\bar T\\mid M)&=\\frac{P(\\bar T\\cap M)}{P(M)}\\\\P(\\bar T\\mid M)&=\\frac{0.32}{0.80}\\\\P(\\bar T\\mid M)&=0.4\\\\P(\\bar T)&=0.4\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $P(\\bar T\\mid M)=P(\\bar T)$, the events are independent.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
